#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A fullscreen picker for tmux, zellij and herdr sessions and the coding
agents that run in them.

Usage: multiplexer-dashboard [--multiplexer tmux|zellij|herdr]
                             [--client CLIENT] [--dir DIR]
                             [--theme auto|light|dark] [--no-bg]
                             [--sidebar]

The left column lists sessions above agents, both grouped by multiplexer in
the order zellij, tmux, herdr. The right side previews the selected
session's focused pane or the selected agent's pane, in that pane's own
colors. Enter switches to the selected session or jumps to the selected
agent's pane, and the dashboard then exits.

Inside a multiplexer, found from the environment variables TMUX, ZELLIJ and
HERDR_ENV=1, the dashboard lists only that multiplexer, or each one it runs
in when nested. Outside any multiplexer it lists every installed one, and a
switch replaces the dashboard with a client that attaches to the session.
--multiplexer limits the list to one multiplexer.

Herdr has no sessions in the sense of tmux, because a herdr session is a
whole server. The dashboard lists the workspaces of the default herdr server
as sessions, as multiplexer-new-session does.

An agent is a pane whose foreground program is one of claude, codex,
opencode, pi, gemini, aider, amp, crush, goose, cursor-agent, qwen, droid and
copilot, or of the comma-separated names in MULTIPLEXER_DASHBOARD_AGENTS.
When the foreground program is an interpreter (node, bun, deno or python),
the name comes from the first argument that is not an option, such as
".../bin/gemini". Herdr reports its own agents and their status. Zellij
0.46 and later report the status that an agent sends with the OSC 7501
escape sequence. Each
detected agent has its own icon, and every other agent has the icon "◇".

New sessions are named as multiplexer-new-session names them: "~" for the
home directory, the name of the repository's root directory inside a git
repository, and the directory name otherwise. A name typed in the dialog
replaces this automatic name. Each character other than a letter, a digit,
"_", "-" or "~" becomes "-", so that a name is valid in all three
multiplexers. When a session with the name exists, the dashboard switches to
it instead. The directory is DIR, or else the current directory, except
inside herdr, where it is the directory of the current pane.

CLIENT is the tmux client to switch inside tmux. It defaults to the client
that tmux picks for the calling process.

--sidebar shows only the two lists, without the header and the preview, for
a narrow pane that stays next to the work, such as one in every tab of a
zellij layout or a tmux split. Inside a multiplexer the dashboard then stays
open after a switch, Escape gives focus back to the last pane (in zellij
and tmux), and q quits. The lists refresh every 2 seconds while the pane
has focus, every 5 seconds while it is on screen without focus,
and not at all while it is hidden, such as in a tab that is not shown. A
hidden pane asks its multiplexer every 3 seconds whether it is on screen
again.

Keys: j/k or the arrows move, g/G or Home/End jump to the ends, Alt+j/k or
Alt+arrows jump between multiplexers, Tab switches lists, Enter switches,
/ filters, n creates, r renames, x kills, Ctrl+L refreshes, ? shows every
key, and q or Escape quits. A click selects a row, a second click switches,
and the wheel moves the cursor.
"""

